yoyo goal set and yoyo init now exit 1 when their write fails, so yoyo goal set x && next-step stops instead of carrying on. The census is posted on #1137. Commit 446cf0e4 is titled "Part of #1137" because two broken verbs are still open. fmt, clippy (-D warnings) and the full cargo test pass.

Census. The script read the verb list from KNOWN_SUBCOMMANDS in src/cli.rs and probed 38 of the 39 verbs; update wasn't run because it replaces the binary in place. Each verb ran in a temp HOME with a fake key, no gh auth, and a read-only project folder and .yoyo/.
• Limit: each verb got one failure condition, so "exit 0, no failure line" doesn't prove the verb never writes. The table showed goal set as clean because the existing goal.md was itself writable. Targeted probes with a read-only goal.md caught it.
• Verbs that printed a failure and exited 0: goal set (both the write and the create-.yoyo/ failure), goal clear, goal verify <cmd>, goal verify clear, init, skill search (gh not authenticated) and skill install (clone failed).
• Comment: it opens with "Scope: still open = skill search, skill install … ; fixed in this slice = goal set, init". It's at issuecomment-6648047240.

Fix.
• goal: all four failing forms run through one handler, so I fixed every write/remove failure in it, not only set. One helper (goal_write_failed in src/commands_goal.rs) prints the error and records the failure, and goal_shell_status turns that into exit 1. That goes slightly beyond the task, which named only goal set. The interactive-session refusal from #982 and the exit 2 for usage errors are unchanged.
• init: handle_init_in (src/commands_project.rs) returns 1 when it can't write YOYO.md. The shell exits with that code, and the REPL ignores it. Leaving an existing YOYO.md or CLAUDE.md alone still exits 0.
• Exit code: 1, because a failed write is a runtime failure, not a usage error (that would be 2).
• Docs: docs/src/usage/commands.md already listed exit codes for goal, so I updated it.

Tests. Five new tests in tests/unknown_flag_refusal.rs run the real binary and reuse its existing env-scrubbing helper.
• Failure cases (exit 1): read-only goal.md (file unchanged), read-only folder with no .yoyo/ (none gets created), goal verify into a read-only .yoyo/, a goal clear that can't remove the file (goal kept), and init in a read-only folder (no YOYO.md).
• Near-misses (must stay exit 0): goal set in a writable folder writes the file, goal clear with no goal, a fresh init, and an init next to an existing YOYO.md leaves it alone.
• Root: the read-only tests skip with a printed reason when file permissions aren't enforced, as under root.
• Positive control: I disabled both new mappings, re-ran, and restored in one step. Exactly the 4 failure tests went red, the near-miss test stayed green, and no NEUTERED marker is left in the file.

Still open on #1137: skill search and skill install (not fixed here, as the task said), and update, which hasn't been probed.
